From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vo_avfoundation: pixel kernels, geometry and buffer pools

Shared helpers for the AVFoundation video output.

pixels.c holds the software upload copies (row copies, U and V interleave,
and the 10-bit and 12-bit shifts into the top bits of each word), the
direct libass and premultiplied BGRA subtitle blends, and the YUV subtitle
composite for biplanar 4:2:0 frames. On arm64 the upload copies and the two
blends are vectorised with NEON, working in 8-bit and 16-bit lanes through
exact integer identities, and give the same bytes as their scalar forms,
which define the results and serve other builds. The composite maps the
subtitle box into frame pixels with one pixel of slack and evaluates its
arithmetic in double precision with explicit fused multiply-adds in a fixed
order, so the result does not depend on the compiler's contraction
settings.

geometry.c computes the host layer's pixel size (a truncated fused
multiply-add of size, scale and 0.5, at least 1) and the frame-space
subtitle canvas used while Picture in Picture composites subtitles.

pool.c creates the output's CoreVideo pools: at least 3 buffers, a maximum
age of 1 s, and Metal-compatible, IOSurface-backed buffers. A pool is
replaced, after flushing its excess buffers, when its size or format
changes.

Applies to mpv v0.41.0 with Vivid's earlier patches.

